[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139628,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoma is a benign tumour arising on the surface of bone and is composed primarily of lamellar mature cortical-type bone. The term &ldquo;bone island&rdquo; is used when an osteoma develops within the medullary cavity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139629,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9180/0 Osteoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139630,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.Z &amp; XH4818 Benign osteogenic tumours of unspecified site &amp; Osteoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139631,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> ivory exostosis; parosteal osteoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139632,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139633,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteomas predominantly affect craniofacial bones formed by membranous ossification {18154576}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139634,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteomas are usually slow growing and asymptomatic {18154576}. On radiological imaging, osteomas are round, dense, well-defined ivory-like lesions which are attached to the underlying bone without cortical invasion. The presence of multiple osteomas suggests the diagnosis of Gardner syndrome {8956591}, which is a subtype of familial adenomatous polyposis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139635,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Since osteomas commonly represent incidental findings, their actual prevalence is difficult to determine but has been reported to reach 6.4% in select case series {25719573}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139636,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of sporadic cases is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139637,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most osteomas develop sporadically and a small subset of cases is associated with Gardner syndrome, a phenotypic variant of familial adenomatous polyposis caused by mutations in the <em>APC</em> gene resulting in aberrant activation of the WNT/&beta;-catenin signalling pathway. In 61.1% of sporadic osteomas, hotspot mutations in the <em>CTNNB1</em> gene (encoding &beta;-catenin) were found {34725446}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139638,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteomas arise on the surface of the bone and are typically well-circumscribed tumours with a broad attachment to the underlying bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139639,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteomas are predominantly composed of mature lamellar/cortical-type bone and can be divided histologically into compact and (less frequent) spongious subtypes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139640,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139641,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139642,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone tumour with compatible imaging; tumour arises on the surface of bone or within the medullary cavity; tumour composed of lamellar/cortical-type bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139643,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139644,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Asymptomatic cases generally do not require treatment and follow an indolent clinical course; symptomatic cases can be conservatively excised.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]